{
  "profileID": "browser-host-v1",
  "designGuidance": {
    "version": "1",
    "rules": [
      "Author for the actual responsive browser viewport in this request. browser-host-v1 is an opt-in host bridge in an opaque-origin sandbox; it is not the native device runtime. Existing offline browser snapshots are a separate unchanged profile.",
      "Use index.html with bundled CSS, classic JavaScript, SVG and local JSON. Keep the existing UTF-8 package/file/path/byte limits. No modules, remote code/fonts/styles, direct remote fetch/XHR/sockets, workers, nested frames, forms or external navigation. Manifest pages may select other bundled HTML documents through the host.",
      "The host supplies window.screenpunk before package scripts. Use only runtime.ready/onStatus, connections.read/release, state.get/set/remove, navigation.get/open and dispose advertised here. Do not replace the bridge or bundle a native transport for newly authored browser screens. Unsupported APIs must show an honest unavailable state.",
      "Only the browser publicHTTP service descriptor may appear in services. Its supported/configured/authorized/entitled/reachable observations are independent yes/no/unknown facts; unknown does not authorize a read. Never infer a grant from runtime status, a declared connection, a backup, a native account or prior package revision. Public reads require an exact declared operation and user approval for this browser screen package revision.",
      "Use the publicHTTP operation descriptor for reviewed origins, string parameters, cache/size/rate limits and returned JSON or image resources. Resource URLs are opaque and browser-managed; release images when replaced and on teardown. Handle CORS, offline, denied, rate-limited and stale responses without fabricating fresh data. Never forward credentials, cookies or caller-controlled headers.",
      "screenpunk.state.get/set/remove is asynchronous JSON state in this browser account and screen, with 16384 bytes per value, 131072 bytes and 128 keys per screen, and host-enforced JSON nesting limits. Missing state resolves to null; await writes and handle failures. State and persistent DOM-storage keys are limited to 256 characters and must not be __proto__, prototype or constructor. State is separate from authoring preferences, screen data and DOM storage, and never accesses state on a native device or another screen.",
      "The host provides scoped localStorage and sessionStorage compatibility methods length/key/getItem/setItem/removeItem/clear. Use these methods rather than named property access. localStorage is hydrated for this browser account/screen and is limited to 524288 bytes; writes update the local projection synchronously and persistence can fail asynchronously. sessionStorage is limited to 524288 bytes and resets on document recreation. No cross-tab storage events or native-device persistence is promised.",
      "Declare optional manifest pages as unique {id,name,path} entries selecting existing bundled HTML files, at most64 pages within the package file limit, and an optional defaultPageId matching a page. navigation.get returns {pageId}; navigation.open changes only to a declared local page, not another saved screen or device. Without pages, the page is default/index.html. No automatic native event rules are advertised.",
      "Call runtime.ready when usable. runtime.onStatus reports lifecycle and adapter availability, not user authorization. Honor document visibility/pagehide, cancel reads and stop timers while inactive, release old image resources and call dispose at teardown. A browser may throttle background timers; there is no always-on native background execution guarantee.",
      "No Home Assistant, Google TV, Calendar, native Maps/cameras/microphones/location, device brightness, authoring preference mutations or screen-data publish/remove/query is implemented by this profile. Requests must have empty preferences and results must not mutate them or introduce screenData declarations. Do not invent provider integrations or inherit native credentials. A configured weather location may remain in bundled package data without requesting browser geolocation.",
      "Preserve semantic HTML, keyboard/focus behavior, image alt text, live status messages and reduced-motion CSS. Do not invent an accessibility SDK namespace. When editing, preserve behavior except requested changes and return results bound to the exact sealed request/digest/base revision."
    ]
  },
  "runtime": {
    "version": "1",
    "packageFormat": "utf8-files-v1",
    "features": [
      "html",
      "css",
      "javascript",
      "bundled-classic-scripts",
      "bundled-local-assets",
      "browser-host-v1",
      "runtime.ready",
      "runtime.onStatus",
      "connections.read",
      "connections.release",
      "state.get",
      "state.set",
      "state.remove",
      "navigation.get",
      "navigation.open",
      "browser.localStorage-v1",
      "browser.sessionStorage-v1",
      "dispose"
    ],
    "limits": {
      "metadataBytes": 131072,
      "requestBytes": 393216,
      "screenBytes": 204800,
      "screenFiles": 20
    }
  },
