            "browserScreenRevisionApproval",
            "reviewedBrowserPublicOrigin"
          ],
          "instructions": "Use await screenpunk.connections.read(alias, operation, parameters, {signal}) for a manifest-defined publicHTTP operation. read is the SDK method, not a literal provider operation. The exact supported origins are https://api.weather.gov, https://mapservices.weather.noaa.gov, https://basemap.nationalmap.gov, https://www.nasa.gov and https://images-assets.nasa.gov; no other host or port is supported by this profile. Declare <=8 connections, <=16 unique operations each, <=12 exact string parameters. Paths are safe absolute ASCII paths without query, fragment, percent encoding, empty, dot or parent segments; parameters are declared query or path values. Names match [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,63} and must not override credentials or destination. Use finite strings, canonical safe-integer ranges, or raster-only pathSegment declarations of <=256 safe ASCII characters. The trusted host performs credential-free, redirect-free public reads; browser CORS or source availability may still reject a request. userAgent is manifest metadata, not a promise that the browser sends a custom User-Agent. JSON <=1MiB, PNG/JPEG <=4MiB and <=4096 each dimension/4194304 pixels. Successful reads return state fresh or stale plus data or an opaque browser-managed resourceURL, fetchedAt and optional lastModified; failures reject with a code. Assign the returned resourceURL to a local image and call screenpunk.connections.release when finished. Never assume a screenpunk: URL or fetch the image URL yourself. Respect <=4 simultaneous reads and <=60 reads/minute; refresh only while visible. maxAgeSeconds is 1..86400 and staleSeconds 0..604800. Current-package authorization does not authorize a newly edited package."
        }
      ],
      "setupInstructions": "Use only the reviewed browser public-data sources and declared operations. The user must allow public data in Viewer Screen Settings for the current screen package revision; no native credentials or approvals are inherited."
